# Value membrane for the capacity contract (closed world — what may cross into the clean
# holon). The pattern is a CONTRACT-AUTHOR DECLARATION: the contract owns per-field
# verification strength, as stem-shapes.ttl already states for its own fields.
#
# THE PATTERN IS ship:total's, BORROWED UNCHANGED. Measured against the capacity page: it admits
# the printed tonnages (10,000 / 12,500 / 14,000) and refuses `Available`, `On Application`, `Y`
# and `N` — the four non-tonnage spellings the page carries in that column. Refusing them is the
# point: they quarantine as propositions rather than being asserted as capacities.
#
# IT ALSO ADMITS A BARE `0`, and that is [[R213]]'s invisible-glyph hazard, named here rather
# than left implicit. MEASURED 2026-09-13, and the figure is not "most" but ALL: every one of the
# 110 cells this page's reading carries as `0` is a glyph whose colour matches the rectangle
# behind it — dark navy on dark navy — so the page shows an EMPTY cell wherever the reading says
# zero. Set identity, not a matching count: 110 of 110, none genuinely printed. A proposer that
# bound those to this field would therefore assert 110 capacities of zero that the page does not
# state. Under the corpus battery's ABSTAINING proposer no unlabelled leaf grounds at all, so the
# hazard is not live in CI; it becomes live the first time a real proposer runs against this
# contract, and it is the reason `capacity` must not be widened to admit an empty reading either.
#
# `year` and `elevationPeriod` carry NO value constraint by design — they ground by exact field
# identity, and a pattern over a period spelling would be the contract inventing a format the
# page does not promise. `port` needs none either: its SKOS scheme membership IS its oracle.
@prefix ship: <https://example.org/shipping#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .

ship:ElevationCapacityShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass ship:ElevationCapacity ;
    sh:property [ sh:path ship:capacity ;
        sh:pattern "^[0-9]{1,3}(,[0-9]{3})*$" ] .
